# A crate, one unit on each side, its base at y = 0 (y points up here, as in any .obj). tools/make_model.py makes
# the game's files from it; crate.mtl gives the sides and lid the texture crate.png and the base a plain colour.
# Every face is wound counter-clockwise seen from outside, the .obj convention. It is one part (`o crate`): with
# crate.rig the model is animated with one joint, as the game's own crates are (the Case class builds an animated body).
mtllib crate.mtl
o crate
v -0.5 0 -0.5
v 0.5 0 -0.5
v 0.5 0 0.5
v -0.5 0 0.5
v -0.5 1 -0.5
v 0.5 1 -0.5
v 0.5 1 0.5
v -0.5 1 0.5
vt 0 0
vt 1 0
vt 1 1
vt 0 1
usemtl wood
f 5/1 8/2 7/3 6/4
f 5/4 6/3 2/2 1/1
f 6/4 7/3 3/2 2/1
f 7/4 8/3 4/2 3/1
f 8/4 5/3 1/2 4/1
usemtl base
f 2 3 4 1
